@*
    Single-glyph line icon for the NieFarm 2.0 redesign — one component, one switch
    over an icon name, rather than 28 tiny components: the SVG path data is the only
    thing that varies between glyphs, so a single switch is the smallest reviewable
    surface (docs/plans/public-site-redesign-nf2.md §5, step 1.4).

    Path data is ported verbatim from the approved design-preview prototype: the eight
    process-stage glyphs (seedling/sprout/shield-leaf/cherries/drop/drying-rack/roaster/
    cup) come from docs/design-preview/quy-trinh.html's ".stage__glyph" markup; the
    shared UI glyphs come from the header/body markup repeated across index.html,
    cua-hang.html and san-pham.html. Glyphs the plan lists with no prototype source
    (chevron-down, close, menu, user, logout, receipt, calendar, location, phone, mail)
    are drawn fresh at the same 24x24 viewBox and stroke weight as the rest. "share" was
    added in Phase 3 (ArticleDetail.razor's share button, step 3.3) for the same reason —
    no prototype source, drawn fresh at the same viewBox/stroke weight. "pause" and "play"
    were added for PartnerMarquee.razor's pause toggle
    (docs/plans/home-partners-marquee.md D11), drawn fresh the same way.

    Not wired into any page yet — Phase 1 only creates the component. It renders
    ".ico" (nf.css) so it inherits currentColor/stroke-width/stroke-linecap from there;
    passing Draw="true" additionally stamps pathLength="1" and a staggered "--d" delay
    on every path/shape directly in markup, so nf-motion.js's own normalisation pass is
    only ever a fallback for hand-written SVG elsewhere (plan §6).
*@
<svg class="ico @(Draw ? "draw" : null) @CssClass"
     width="@Size" height="@Size" viewBox="@_viewBox"
     stroke-width="@StrokeWidth.ToString(System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)"
     aria-hidden="@(AriaHidden ? "true" : "false")">
    @_content
</svg>

@code {
    /// <summary>Glyph name — see the switch below for the supported set.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Name { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>Rendered width/height in pixels (the SVG is square).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public int Size { get; set; } = 20;

    [Parameter]
    public double StrokeWidth { get; set; } = 1.4;

    /// <summary>Stamps pathLength="1" + a staggered --d delay on every path/shape so
    /// nf.css's ".draw" self-drawing animation can run on this glyph.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Draw { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>False for glyphs that carry their own visible label (e.g. inside a
    /// button whose text already names the action) — otherwise this is a decorative
    /// glyph and stays hidden from assistive tech.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool AriaHidden { get; set; } = true;

    private string _viewBox = "0 0 24 24";
    private MarkupString _content;

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        var (viewBox, elements) = Glyph(Name);
        _viewBox = viewBox;

        var sb = new System.Text.StringBuilder();
        for (var i = 0; i < elements.Length; i++)
            sb.Append(Draw ? WithDrawAttributes(elements[i], i) : elements[i]);

        // Safe as MarkupString: every value returned by Glyph() below is a compile-time
        // constant selected from a fixed table by Name — nothing here is built from
        // request/user input (a different case from article and activity bodies, which
        // are sanitised server-side before rendering; see CLAUDE.md's MarkupString safety note).
        _content = new MarkupString(sb.ToString());
    }

    private static string WithDrawAttributes(string element, int index)
    {
        var delay = System.Math.Min(index * 0.11, 1.2)
            .ToString("0.##", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
        var insertion = $" pathLength=\"1\" style=\"--d:{delay}s\"";
        var closeTagIndex = element.LastIndexOf("/>", System.StringComparison.Ordinal);
        return closeTagIndex < 0 ? element : element.Insert(closeTagIndex, insertion);
    }

